<%# System status (design spec §6.1, Task 9; round 3): the setup wizard's own
    `Setup::SystemCheck` results, through the same row component, so both
    screens word every check identically. "Run checks again" is a plain GET
    back to this screen, which re-runs every check -- idempotent, so a reload
    does the same. The time is the site's (`Admin::BaseController` runs every
    request in the site time zone). %>
<% content_for :title, "System status" %>
<% passed = @results.count(&:ok?) %>
<div class="max-w-[900px]">
  <div class="mb-4 flex flex-wrap items-start justify-between gap-3">
    <div>
      <h1 class="text-h1 text-ink">System status</h1>
      <p class="mt-1 text-meta"><%= passed %> of <%= @results.size %> checks passed · last run <%= Time.zone.now.strftime("%H:%M") %></p>
    </div>
    <%= link_to "Run checks again", admin_system_status_path(**admin_url_options), class: setup_secondary_link_class,
          data: { turbo_prefetch: "false" } %>
  </div>

  <%= render "setup/system_check_results", results: @results, copyable: true %>
</div>
